## About the exhibition

The Brightwater Maritime Museum is pleased to present *Tides of Trade*, an exhibition that follows spice, tea and cotton routes between 1600 and 1850. Visitors will meet the trade through original ship ledgers, navigation instruments and a full-size reconstruction of a cargo hold.

The centerpiece is the 1783 log of the brig *Hesper*, shown publicly for the first time.

## Visiting

